    "body": "Copied from #461 comment by @1472583610.\n\n### Contact Details (e.g. Tox ID or email)\n\n_No response_\n\n### qTox Version\n\n_No response_\n\n### Commit Hash\n\n_No response_\n\n### Toxcore Version\n\n_No response_\n\n### Qt Version\n\n_No response_\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nCreate a group chat, close all chat windows, hide the contact list to tray (I'm using separate windows), have a message sent to the group chat. The \"Notify via desktop notifications\" setting is disabled. The \"Open window\" option is enabled.\n\n### Observed Behavior\n\nThe contact list automatically opens when a message arrives. The tray icon flashes. The group chat window remains closed.\n\n### Expected Behavior\n\nThe group chat window should automatically open as it does for 1-on-1 chats. Focus should not be set to the group chat window so that the taskbar button can flash until the message is read.\n\n### Reproducibility\n\nUnable to reproduce\n\n### Operating System\n\nWindows\n\n### Operating System version/distro/name/etc.\n\nWindows 10\n\n### Relevant log output\n\n```shell\n\n```",
